  "title": "Timestamps on messages - need improvement?",
  "content": "<p>In general, I hate when things do this:</p><figure><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://uploads-eu-west-1.insided.com/stmicroelectronics-en/attachment/55f7677f-ae3f-4fbf-83f4-29d41bce1033.png\" /></figure><p> </p><p>Just tell me the actual date!</p><p> </p><p>But, if you <em>are </em>going to do it, make it accurate:</p><figure><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://uploads-eu-west-1.insided.com/stmicroelectronics-en/attachment/730cee7b-9b94-414e-8a70-aeee4b773f4a.png\" /></figure><p> </p><oembed url=\"https://community.st.com/feedback-forum-118/forced-password-reset-136604\"></oembed><p> </p><p>To meaningfully reflect the actual date, that should say <strong>two</strong> years ago!</p><p>If it’s going to talk in years, then the value needs to be to the <em><strong>nearest</strong> </em>year.</p><p> </p><p>Or just show both ?</p>",
